"The Greenbrier Companies, Inc. designs, manufactures, and markets railroad freight car equipment in North America, Europe, and South America. It operates through Manufacturing, and Leasing & Management Services segments. The Manufacturing segment offers covered hopper cars, gondolas, open top hoppers, boxcars, center partition cars, tank cars, sustainable conversions, intermodal railcars, and railcar equipment; reconditioning of wheels and axles, new axle machining, finishing, and downsizing; operates a railcar maintenance network; and reconditions and manufactures railcar cushioning units, couplers, yokes, side frames, bolsters, and various other parts. The Leasing & Management Services segment offers operating leases and per diem leases for a fleet of approximately 20,900 railcars; and management services comprising railcar maintenance management, railcar accounting services, fleet management and logistics, administration, and railcar remarketing. This segment provides management services for railroads, shippers, carriers, institutional investors, and other leasing and transportation companies. It serves railroads, leasing companies, financial institutions, shippers, carriers, and transportation companies. The company was founded in 1919 and is headquartered in Lake Oswego, Oregon.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Lorie L. Tekorius | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $246K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Greenbrier Companies, Inc. (The is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.3B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -15% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 7% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 14% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $240M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 8.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 92% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9228990265271988},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (GBX) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/8/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_GBX_Price_Events_111126121201_1794417121.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794417121.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Greenbrier (GBX) Stock May Still Be Undervalued On Earnings","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/greenbrier-gbx-stock-may-still-130952309.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794316192.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Greenbrier Companies (GBX) Reports Weaker Full Year Results, Is The Upside Already Priced In?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-gbx/greenbrier-companies/news/greenbrier-companies-gbx-reports-weaker-full-year-results-is","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794162171.642,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.807,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Greenbrier Companies (GBX) Just Gave Investors Something To Think About","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/